What CoreGS is
--------------

CoreGS is a hardware-faithful PlayStation 2 Graphics Synthesizer renderer for Vulkan.

Origin
------

CoreGS was extracted from GT4Recomp (https://github.com/moesuito/gt4-staticrecomp), a static
recompilation of Gran Turismo 4, at commit ebfe1ca5 (branch release/1.3.0-rc15, 2026-11-06). The
renderer there is called CoreGS 2.0 and was written from GT4Recomp's own clean-room specification of
the PS2 GS hardware. This repository keeps that code, removes the Gran Turismo 4 content rules from
the generic core (they now live in profiles/gt4 as an example) and publishes the renderer on its
own.

No game data, no disc image, no BIOS, no save, no capture and no game executable is part of this
repository.

Clean room
----------

CoreGS is a clean-room implementation: it was written from the PS2 hardware documentation and from
observing the GS register and packet interfaces, not from the source of another emulator or renderer.
No GPL code and no code or text derived from another emulator is included. See CONTRIBUTING.md for
the rule contributors must follow.

